# Docs Trust Tiers

## Planning sources (high trust)

- `docs/ai/ACTIVE_WORK.md`
- `docs/ai/FEATURE_REGISTRY.md` (In Progress / Planned)
- `docs/ai/TECH_DEBT.md` (Open)
- recent `docs/ai/PROGRESS_LOG.md`
- code, tests, and verify commands (`docs/Verification.md`)

## Product truth (dual-track; architecture guidance, not auto-backlog)

- `docs/` architecture/conventions/verification
- root `AGENTS.md` ownership and lightweight daily-fix rules
- Use for how the system works; do **not** turn ROADMAP tables into the active queue until registered in `FEATURE_REGISTRY.md`

## Reference sources (do not auto-create backlog)

- old roadmap files (including `Infrastructure/ROADMAP.md` until a Feature is registered)
- docs explicitly marked Snapshot, Archived, or Reference
- stale unchecked checklist sections in historical design docs

## Conflict resolution

If docs conflict with runtime truth, code/tests/verification outputs take precedence.
